I took a random character for a change of pace, and was given a chaotic
monk.  Hmm.  Well, OK.

Down to sokoban, and up.  And what should be at the top but a wand of 
wishing.  Gee, how nice.

Moments after wresting out the sixth and final wish, it occurred to me
that I'd left reflection off the list.  Whoops.

Oddly, this didn't lead to my demise.

My little dog had been turned into a white dragon before sokoban, and
off to minetown.  Not much left there but the priest and candle
salesman.  Down further, and my dragon got turned into a Troll.  OK, I
can live with that.

Then, with my ring of cold resistance in my bag of holding, I kicked
myself to death on a blue jelly . . . *sigh*

This of course followed the gnomish healer who discovered that a
floating eye can give 17 XP (???), and had a more limited chat in
minetown.

And the wizard that was doing nicely . . .

But, hey, a co-aligned temple with a brown pudding stalking me! 

So I expanded the temple (it was that new minetown with rock around the
upper temple), and set my hand to agriculture.  In time, I became
curious about the scrolls, so headed off to the general store to check
and see if I'd found an ID.

So there were lots of pesky critters to clean up; still not much of a
problem.  

Oh, a pyrolisk; put on the blindfold. Kill it, and a couple of giants.
Keep smacking away.  That wand wasn't hurting me, but I wanted the 
charges.  Step forward--right into the square where I'd just killed a
cockatrice . . .

